# 10xProductivity — .env at repo root (gitignored)
#
# Do NOT copy a giant template here. Each tool documents its own variables in:
#   tool_connections/{tool}/setup.md   (and connection-*.md for details)
#
# During setup, the agent appends only the blocks for tools you connect.
#
# Create an empty file to start:
#   touch .env
#
# Or copy this single line if your shell needs a file to exist:
# # (add variables from each tool's setup.md as you connect them)
#
# --- Local repo shortcuts (optional) ---
# Parent directory for your clones. Defaults to $HOME/code if unset when you source repo_paths.sh.
# CODE_HOME=/path/to/your/code
#
# Shell aliases for common projects (10x ↔ 10xProductivity, eddg ↔ EDDG-RDA, collab ↔ collaboration-station):
#   source tool_connections/repo_paths.sh
# Then: cd "$REPO_10X"  or  cd "$REPO_EDDG"  or  cd "$REPO_COLLAB"
#
# If you cannot source bash (only flat KEY=value in .env), duplicate full paths:
# REPO_10XPRODUCTIVITY=/path/to/your/code/10xProductivity
# REPO_10X=/path/to/your/code/10xProductivity
# REPO_EDDG_RDA=/path/to/your/code/EDDG-RDA
# REPO_EDDG=/path/to/your/code/EDDG-RDA
# REPO_COLLABORATION_STATION=/path/to/your/code/collaboration-station
# REPO_COLLAB=/path/to/your/code/collaboration-station
